              domain."

Why this commit and not 727ab8eb (hUGETracker's default branch head, 3fedced3,
moved its submodule there on 2026-08-15): 727ab8eb reads a new song descriptor
(four tick bytes for grooves, then the order count as a byte), but hUGETracker's
RGBDS export at 3fedced3 still writes the old one (one tick byte, then a pointer
to the order count), so that commit's own export doesn't play on it. a3cbd0ce is
the newest driver the export (codegen.pas `RenderSongToRGBDSAsm`, which
crates/music/src/asm.rs ports) is written for. See
project/2026-11-07-music-build.md.

The files are committed unmodified. `gbcli new` writes hUGEDriver.asm to a new
project's src/ and the two .inc files to its include/ (crates/build/src/scaffold.rs
embeds them with include_str!); the driver's own `include "include/hardware.inc"`
finds the project's gbdev hardware.inc, which defines every name it uses.
crates/build/tests/it/scaffold.rs checks the embedded bytes against the sha256s
above. To update: fetch the files at a newer commit the same way, check that
hUGETracker's export at the matching tracker commit still writes the descriptor
the driver reads, update this file and the emitter, and re-run the build tests.
